INT. ROTATING RESTAURANT - TOWER SUMMIT - NIGHT

A circular room on a slow turn. The city slides past the windows like a conveyor. White tablecloths, empty chairs, a pianist's bench with no pianist.

ROZ KAPLAN, 50s, silver bob, red lipstick, sits at a corner table with a blueprint under her wine glass. Opposite her, TREVOR DUNN, 30s, hotel uniform, nervous hands.

A NEW GIRL, 20s, denim jacket, backpack, slides into the third chair without being invited.

NEW GIRL
Sorry I'm late. The elevator stopped at every floor.

ROZ
It's a tourist elevator.

NEW GIRL
It was a hostage situation.

ROZ
You've got the codes?

NEW GIRL
I've got the codes.

TREVOR
Who is she?

ROZ
Trevor, this is Sunny Lockwood. She's the one I told you about.

SUNNY
Nice to meet you. I'm the one with the thumbs.

TREVOR
The thumbs?

SUNNY
Locksmith's daughter. Four generations of thumbs.

ROZ
She's good. She's very good. She's also nineteen.

TREVOR
Twenty-one.

SUNNY
Twenty. Don't lie for me.

ROZ
Let's start. The vault is on sixty-one, under the observation deck. Every ninety minutes the restaurant makes a full revolution. We have exactly four minutes where the north camera faces the wall.

TREVOR
Because of the rotation.

ROZ
Because of the rotation. Sunny takes the first lock. I take the second. Trevor, you stay at the maitre d' stand and pour wine.

TREVOR
I can pour wine.

ROZ
You can pour wine badly. That's all anyone expects.

SUNNY
What's the haul?

ROZ
Eleven million. Bearer bonds. In a briefcase that looks like a briefcase.

SUNNY
Eleven's good. What's my cut?

ROZ
Two.

SUNNY
Three.

ROZ
Two and a half.

SUNNY
She drives a hard bargain.

TREVOR
She who?

SUNNY
Roz. It's a figure of speech. I'm talking about Roz.

ROZ
I know who you mean.

SUNNY
She counts every penny.

ROZ
She buys every drink. Shut up and listen.

Trevor pours wine for no one. The glass fills. He sets the bottle down too hard.

ROZ (CONT'D)
After the second lock, there's a pneumatic tube. Documents only. We use it to send the bonds down to the kitchen.

TREVOR
They go down by tube.

ROZ
They go down by tube. At the kitchen, Marguerite takes them in a casserole dish.

SUNNY
Who's Marguerite?

ROZ
My sister.

SUNNY
You have a sister?

ROZ
Everyone has a sister.

TREVOR
I don't.

ROZ
Then you're lucky.

SUNNY
What about security?

ROZ
Two guards. One reads novels. The other sleeps. We tested them for six weeks.

SUNNY
Six weeks of watching a man read a novel.

ROZ
It was a Dickens.

SUNNY
Which?

ROZ
Bleak House.

SUNNY
(laughing)
Oh, I like her.

TREVOR
Who?

SUNNY
Roz. You keep asking.

ROZ
Pay attention. Revolution starts at eleven forty. We're in position by eleven thirty. Questions?

TREVOR
What if the guard doesn't sleep?

ROZ
Then I buy him a drink.

SUNNY
What if he doesn't drink?

ROZ
Everyone drinks, sweetheart.

SUNNY
What if the vault door is a different model?

ROZ
It isn't.

SUNNY
What if it is?

ROZ
Then you'll earn your three.

SUNNY
(grinning)
Three?

ROZ
Two and a half. Don't push.

The room turns. The city lights drift past, one landmark after another.

TREVOR
It's a little beautiful, actually.

ROZ
It's a job, Trevor.

TREVOR
Can it be both?

ROZ
No.

Sunny lifts her glass. Roz clinks it. Trevor, last, doesn't quite reach.
